{"file_path":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/finite_spectral_shadows.tex","new_string":"The finite-operator side is now largely a theorem. \\cref{thm:class} classifies\nthe coboundaries; \\cref{cor:strict} gives a strict gap at every finite level;\n\\cref{thm:collapse} reduces uniformity in $Q$ to a single sequence of computable\nconstants. What remains open is one statement about that sequence.\n\n\\begin{keystatement}\nThis work identifies the correct operator (the faithful \\texttt{sync}\nsynchronized operator), \\emph{proves} the correct quotient\n($\\operatorname{Cob}=\\langle\\chi_2\\rangle$, \\cref{thm:class}), proves a strict\nnon-coboundary gap at every finite level (\\cref{cor:strict}), and proves that the\nuniform gap is governed by the $r$-independent conductor sequence\n$\\gamma_c(s)$ (\\cref{thm:collapse}):\n\\[\n\\kappa_{3^r}(s)=1-\\max_{2\\le c\\le r}\\gamma_c(s),\\qquad\n\\gamma_c(s)<1\\ \\text{for every }c .\n\\]\nThe single remaining finite-operator statement is that\n$\\sup_c\\gamma_c(s)<1$.\n\\end{keystatement}\n\n\\noindent\\textbf{Proof status.}\n\\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.6em,itemsep=1pt]\n\\item \\emph{Proved:} $\\chi_2$ is an exact coboundary (\\cref{thm:cobound});\n$\\operatorname{Cob}=\\langle\\chi_2\\rangle$ on the residue--parity skew product\n(\\cref{thm:class}); strict gap $\\rho(\\Lcal_\\chi)<\\rho(\\Lcal_{\\mathbf1})$ at every\nfinite level for every non-coboundary $\\chi$ and tilt (\\cref{cor:strict});\nconductor autonomy and collapse (\\cref{prop:cond,thm:collapse}); the\nheight-strip rotation identity (\\cref{prop:rot}); the residue-only $\\chi_2$\nratio $\\tfrac{2^{1+s}-1}{2^{1+s}+1}$ (\\cref{prop:dich}).\n\\item \\emph{Open (bounded-conductor extremality):} $\\sup_c\\gamma_c(s)<1$\n(\\cref{conj:ext}). Computed through $c=6$: the sequence peaks at a fixed small\nconductor and decays.\n\\item \\emph{Open (strip classification):} the non-product-form coboundary\nclassification for the killed strip (the residue--parity case is settled;\nproduct-form strip potentials are excluded numerically for $r\\le4$).\n\\item \\emph{Conditional:} a constant sync-quotient gap (\\cref{cor:const}).\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\begin{conjecture}[Bounded-conductor extremality]\\label{conj:ext}\nFor each tilt $s\\in[0,1]$ the sequence $\\gamma_c(s)$ of \\cref{thm:collapse}\nattains its supremum at a fixed finite conductor:\n$\\sup_{c\\ge2}\\gamma_c(s)=\\max_{c\\le c_0}\\gamma_c(s)<1$. Numerically\n$c_0=3$ ($s{=}0$) and $c_0=4$ ($s{=}1$) for the residue--parity operator\n(through $c=6$), and $c_0=2$ for the killed strip at $s=0$ (through $c=5$, where\nthe sequence is monotone decreasing). Caution: monotonicity in $c$ \\emph{fails}\nfor the residue--parity operator ($\\gamma_4>\\gamma_2$ at $s{=}1$), so the correct\ntarget is boundedness/extremality, not monotonicity.\n\\end{conjecture}\n\n\\begin{corollary}[Conditional constant gap]\\label{cor:const}\nAssume \\cref{conj:ext}. Then for all $Q=3^r$ ($r\\ge2$) and $s\\in[0,1]$,\n\\[\n\\rho(\\Lcal_{s,Q,\\chi})\\le(1-\\kappa_0(s))\\,\\rho(\\Lcal_{s,Q,\\mathbf1}),\n\\qquad \\chi\\notin\\langle\\chi_2\\rangle,\n\\qquad\n\\kappa_0(s)=1-\\max_{c\\le c_0}\\gamma_c(s)>0,\n\\]\na \\emph{constant} determined by finitely many computable operators. For the\nresidue--parity operator the computed values give\n$\\kappa_0(0)=1-0.7638=0.2362$ and $\\kappa_0(1)=1-0.9264=0.0736$; for the killed\nstrip at $s=0$, $\\kappa_0=1-0.9069=0.0931$. This is stronger than the fall-back\ntarget $\\kappa_Q\\gg1/\\mathrm{polylog}(Q)$, for which it suffices that\n$\\gamma_c\\le1-c^{-A}$ for some $A$.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\nImmediate from \\cref{thm:collapse}: $\\kappa_{3^r}=1-\\max_{2\\le c\\le r}\\gamma_c$,\nand under \\cref{conj:ext} the maximum is attained at $c\\le c_0$, independent of\n$r$. Each $\\gamma_c<1$ by \\cref{cor:strict} applied at level $3^c$.\n\\end{proof}\n\n\\paragraph{Proof program for \\cref{conj:ext}.} The natural route is\nDoeblin/block minorisation by \\emph{principal-unit cancellation}: for each\nnon-coboundary $\\chi$ of conductor $3^c$, exhibit from every state a finite\nadmissible block family carrying untwisted mass $\\ge\\alpha$ (uniform in $c$) on\nwhich $\\lvert\\E[\\chi(\\text{endpoint})]\\rvert\\le1-\\eta$ with $\\eta$ uniform in\n$c$. Where the block images contain a full coset of a subgroup $H$ with\n$\\chi|_H\\ne1$, cancellation is exact ($\\sum_{u\\in H}\\chi(uh)=0$); high-conductor\ncharacters oscillate faster on the principal-unit filtration, which is the\nmechanism behind the observed decay of $\\gamma_c$ beyond the extremal conductor.\nTo transfer the cancellation into the killed strip, build block families with\nidentical valuation multisets (then the height weights match exactly), or prove\nbounded distortion $w_s(w_1)/w_s(w_2)\\in[C^{-1},C]$ together with QSD bulk\nretention up to $O(e^{-cL})$.","old_string":"The operator question is settled in form; the remaining content is a precise\nquantitative gap on the coboundary quotient.\n\n\\begin{keystatement}\nThis work identifies the correct operator (the faithful \\texttt{sync}\nresidue--height operator) and the correct quotient (by the coboundary subgroup\n$\\langle\\chi_2\\rangle$). The remaining operator theorem is the quantitative\n\\emph{non-coboundary} gap on that quotient.\n\\end{keystatement}\n\n\\noindent\\textbf{Proof status.}\n\\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.6em,itemsep=1pt]\n\\item \\emph{Proved:} the quadratic character is an exact coboundary\n(\\cref{thm:cobound}); conductor sectors are autonomous (\\cref{prop:cond}); the\nresidue-only $\\chi_2$ ratio is $\\tfrac{2^{1+s}-1}{2^{1+s}+1}$ (\\cref{prop:dich}).\n\\item \\emph{Open (coboundary classification):} that $\\langle\\chi_2\\rangle$ is the\n\\emph{whole} coboundary group.\n\\item \\emph{Open (conductor monotonicity):} that no higher-conductor sector\nexceeds the conductor-$9$ ratio.\n\\item \\emph{Conditional:} a constant sync-quotient gap.\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\begin{proposition}[Forward coboundary containment]\\label{prop:cobcontain}\n$\\langle\\chi_2\\rangle$ is contained in the coboundary group of the synchronized\noperator.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\cref{thm:cobound}.\n\\end{proof}\n\n\\begin{conjecture}[No further coboundaries]\\label{conj:nocob}\nNo principal-unit character is a coboundary of the synchronized operator;\nequivalently $\\langle\\chi_2\\rangle$ is exactly the coboundary group. By\nWielandt's equality theorem this is the assertion that\n$\\rho(\\Lcal_{\\chi})<\\rho(\\Lcal_{\\mathbf1})$ for all $\\chi\\notin\\langle\\chi_2\\rangle$;\nit reduces to showing the principal-unit functional equation\n$\\psi(3a+1)=\\psi(a^2)$ on $C=1+3\\Z/3^r$ has no nontrivial solution (it already\nfails at $r=2$). Verified numerically over the full character group for\n$Q\\le3^4$.\n\\end{conjecture}\n\n\\begin{conjecture}[Conductor monotonicity]\\label{conj:mono}\nAmong non-coboundary sectors, the maximal gap ratio occurs at conductor $9$.\nVerified numerically for $Q\\le3^5$ and $s\\in\\{0,1\\}$.\n\\end{conjecture}\n\n\\begin{corollary}[Conditional constant gap]\\label{cor:const}\nAssume \\cref{conj:nocob,conj:mono}. Then for all $Q=3^r$ ($r\\ge2$) and\n$s\\in[0,1]$,\n\\[\n\\rho(\\Lcal^{\\mathrm{sync}}_{s,Q,\\chi})\\le(1-\\kappa_0)\\,\n\\rho(\\Lcal^{\\mathrm{sync}}_{s,Q,\\mathbf1}),\n\\qquad \\chi\\notin\\langle\\chi_2\\rangle,\n\\]\nwith $\\kappa_0=1-0.9069\\approx0.0931$ the gap of the fixed conductor-$9$ operator.\nIn particular $\\kappa_Q^{\\mathrm{sync}/\\mathrm{cob}}\\ge\\kappa_0>0$, stronger than\nthe fall-back target $\\kappa_Q\\gg1/\\mathrm{polylog}(Q)$.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\nBy \\cref{prop:cond} each conductor-$3^c$ sector's ratio is $r$-independent; by\n\\cref{conj:mono} the maximum over non-coboundary sectors is attained at conductor\n$9$, whose operator is fixed and has ratio $0.9069$; by \\cref{conj:nocob} there\nare no other zero-gap sectors. The bound holds for every non-coboundary $\\chi$\nuniformly in $r$.\n\\end{proof}\n\n\\paragraph{Proof program for \\cref{conj:mono}.} The natural route is\nDoeblin/block minorisation by \\emph{principal-unit cancellation}: for each\nnon-coboundary $\\chi$, exhibit from every bulk state a finite admissible block\nfamily carrying untwisted mass $\\ge\\alpha$ on which\n$\\lvert\\E[\\chi(\\text{endpoint})]\\rvert\\le1-\\eta$. Where the block images contain a\nfull coset of a subgroup $H$ with $\\chi|_H\\ne1$, cancellation is exact\n($\\sum_{u\\in H}\\chi(uh)=0$)---the likely source of the observed flat, conductor-\nmonotone gap. A height/QSD transfer step (the synchronized weights on paired\nblocks are comparable, $w_s(w_1)/w_s(w_2)\\in[C^{-1},C]$ uniformly for\n$s\\in[0,1]$, and the blocks remain in the QSD bulk up to $O(e^{-cL})$) carries the\nresidue cancellation into the killed sync operator.","replace_all":false}